<PageLayout title="About HS GPA Calc | Free High School GPA Calculator" description="Learn why HS GPA Calc exists: a free, private high school GPA calculator for weighted and unweighted GPA with AP, Honors, IB and Dual Enrollment classes." path="/about/" heading="About HS GPA Calc">
  <p>HS GPA Calc is a free high school GPA calculator built for students, parents and counselors who want a fast, clear answer to one question: what is my GPA?</p>
  <h2>What we built</h2>
  <p>Add your classes by year, choose a letter grade, credits and class level (Regular, Honors, AP, IB or Dual Enrollment), and see your weighted and unweighted GPA update instantly. You can also see a GPA for each year, your cumulative GPA, and what grades you need to reach a target.</p>
  <h2>Privacy first</h2>
  <p>Everything runs in your browser. Your grades are saved in your own browser storage so they're still there when you come back, and they are never sent to a server. There are no accounts and no sign-up.</p>
  <h2>A note on accuracy</h2>
  <p>Schools calculate GPA in different ways. Our defaults (Honors +0.5, AP/IB/Dual Enrollment +1.0) are common, and you can change them to match your school. Treat results as an estimate and check your official transcript for the number colleges will see.</p>
  <p>Questions or feedback? <a href="/contact/">Contact us</a>.</p>
</PageLayout>
